+---
+id: task-003-fix-single-use-coupon-release-on-cancel-and-free-shipping-at-50-euro
+type: task
+title: "Fix single-use coupon release on cancel and free shipping at 50 euro"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+<!-- task body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold, setting only `id`, `title` and
+     `status` (and any `--tags` or `--set` value). Fill the required frontmatter fields and replace
+     these placeholder comments yourself; `wingfoil memory submit` then checks the required fields,
+     moves `status` forward and commits the document as you left it, naming in the commit body the
+     content it carries. -->
+
+## Request
+
+Two reports: (1) a single-use welcome coupon was refused as already used after the order that used it
+was cancelled; (2) €4.90 shipping charged on goods of exactly €50.00.
+
+## Outcome
+
+1. Fixed: `Orders.cancel` gave the coupon back under the customer's name instead of the order id, so
+   the coupon was never released. It now passes the order id. Test added in `test/orders.test.ts`.
+2. Not reproduced: `shippingCost` already ships free at goods >= €50.00 (existing test covers exactly
+   €50.00). Per the README the threshold looks at goods after every discount and before VAT, so an
+   order whose lines were €50.00 before a discount, or €50.00 only with VAT, is correctly charged.
+   No code change; the exact order is needed to investigate further.
